#: admin/views/scan.php:266
msgid "I found a Critical issue — what should I do first?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:270
msgid ""
"Critical findings represent the highest risk and should be addressed "
"immediately. Common critical issues and first steps:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:272
msgid ""
"wp-config.php or a .env file readable from the web — block access to it, "
"then change the database password and any keys it contains"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:273
msgid "Backup file in the web root — move it out of the web root or delete it"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:274
msgid ""
"PHP file in the uploads folder — find out what added it; uploads should not "
"contain PHP code, and an unknown file there is a common sign of a compromise"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:275
msgid ""
"User with an empty password — set a strong password or remove the account"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:276
msgid "Expired SSL certificate — renew it"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:278
msgid ""
"Open the full report and click each Critical finding for step-by-step fix "
"instructions."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:284
msgid "Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:290
msgid "Can I use this on a staging or local site?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:294
msgid ""
"Yes, but some checks require a publicly accessible HTTPS URL to work "
"correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:296
msgid ""
"SSL/TLS certificate checks will be skipped if the site is on HTTP or uses a "
"self-signed cert"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:297
msgid ""
"HTTP header checks probe the live homepage — localhost URLs are not "
"reachable from the server itself in some configurations"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:298
msgid ""
"Directory listing probes and sensitive file checks rely on HTTP responses"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:300
msgid ""
"All code-level checks (file integrity, permissions, user accounts, PHP "
"config) work fully on any environment."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:307
msgid "Does the scanner work on WordPress multisite?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/scan.php:311
msgid ""
"Yes. On multisite only super admins can run a scan. It checks the shared "
"core files, every installed plugin and theme, and all network users; site "
"settings are read from the site whose dashboard you run it from. ShieldScope "
"is also in the Network Admin menu."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:14
msgid "ShieldScope: Settings"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:24
msgid "Server load"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: preset name, 2: scan pace percent, 3: seconds per step
#: admin/views/settings.php:33
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s: %2$d%%, %3$d s per step"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:37
msgid "Custom (use the two fields below)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:39
msgid ""
"Sets the scan pace and time per step together. Choose Custom to set them "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:44
msgid "Scan pace (share of time working)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:49
msgid ""
"The scanner works in short steps with pauses between them. This is the share "
"of time spent working: lower values mean longer pauses and a slower scan. It "
"is not a CPU limit. Default 20%."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:54
msgid "Time per step (seconds)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:58
msgid ""
"How long one step of the scan may run before it saves its place and stops. "
"Lower this if scans time out. Default 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:63
msgid "Skip files larger than (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:74
msgid ""
"Very large PHP files are usually bundled libraries or generated code and are "
"slow to pattern-check. Skipped files are counted in the report. Accepted "
"range: 1–20 MB. Default 2 MB."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:79
msgid "Background scanning"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:84
msgid "Keep scanning when the scan page is closed (uses WP-Cron)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:86
msgid ""
"WP-Cron runs when the site gets visits (or from a server cron job), so on a "
"quiet site a background scan can take longer. With the scan page open, it "
"runs at full pace either way."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:91
msgid "Pause when tab is hidden"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:96
msgid ""
"Pause the scan while you switch tabs or minimise the window (only when "
"background scanning is off)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:102
msgid "Developer review"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:107
msgid ""
"Also scan plugin and theme code for injection and server-side request "
"patterns."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:109
msgid ""
"For developers reviewing code. These checks only find patterns to review "
"(Low findings), and well-written plugins can match them, so they are off by "
"default. Scans take longer when this is on."
msgstr ""

