#: admin/views/settings.php:187
msgid "What is the WPScan API key and do I need one?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:191
msgid ""
"WPScan keeps a database of known vulnerabilities in WordPress plugins and "
"themes. A key is optional."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:193
msgid ""
"Without a key: only a limited built-in list of widely used plugins is "
"checked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:194
msgid ""
"With a key: each plugin listed on WordPress.org, and the active theme, is "
"looked up on WPScan by its slug."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:196
msgid ""
"The free key allows 25 requests a day and is licensed for non-commercial "
"use. If a site has more plugins than the daily limit, the report says how "
"many could not be checked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:203
msgid "What's the difference between the built-in CVE list and the WPScan API?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of plugins, 2: date the list was last reviewed (YYYY-MM-DD)
#: admin/views/settings.php:211
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The built-in list covers %1$d widely used plugins and was last reviewed on "
"%2$s. It needs no key and no network access, but it is not a vulnerability "
"database: plugins outside the list are not checked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:217
msgid ""
"WPScan covers far more plugins and themes and is updated as new "
"vulnerabilities are published. When a key is set, the built-in list still "
"runs as well."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:224
msgid "How many API requests does each scan use?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:228
msgid ""
"One request per plugin listed on WordPress.org, plus one for the active "
"theme (and its parent theme, if any). Results are cached for 24 hours, so a "
"second scan on the same day uses no extra requests."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:229
msgid ""
"Example: a site with 20 plugins and 2 active themes uses 22 requests on the "
"first scan of the day, and zero on any subsequent scan that day."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:235
msgid "Performance Settings"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:241
msgid "What does the scan pace setting do?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:245
msgid ""
"The scanner works in short steps with pauses between them. The setting is "
"the share of time spent working: at 20%, each step is followed by a pause "
"about four times as long. Lower values spread the work out on a busy server "
"but make the scan slower. It does not measure or cap CPU use."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:247
msgid "10–15%: busy shared hosting"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:248
msgid "20% (default): most sites"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:249
msgid "30–40%: a VPS or managed WordPress hosting, for a faster scan"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:257
msgid "What does Time per step do?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:261
msgid ""
"Each step is one request from this browser tab to your server. This setting "
"caps how long one step can run before it saves its place and stops."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:263
msgid ""
"1–2 seconds — use on servers with strict PHP max_execution_time (common on "
"basic shared hosting)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:264
msgid "2 seconds (default) — works on most hosts"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:265
msgid ""
"5–10 seconds — faster scans on permissive or managed hosting environments"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:273
msgid "What does \"Skip files larger than\" do?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:277
msgid ""
"The code checks read PHP files into memory to look for patterns that need a "
"review (for example eval() on decoded data). Files over this size are "
"skipped."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:278
msgid ""
"Very large PHP files are mostly bundled libraries or generated code. "
"Skipping them saves time and memory, but they are then not checked: the "
"report counts skipped files so you know. The default of 2 MB suits most "
"sites."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:285
msgid "My scan is very slow or keeps timing out — what can I do?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:289
msgid "Try these in order:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:291
msgid "Reduce Time per step to 1 second to avoid PHP timeouts"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:292
msgid "Lower the scan pace to spread the work out"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:293
msgid "Reduce \"Skip files larger than\" to 1 MB to scan fewer large files"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:294
msgid ""
"Run the scan during off-peak hours (night-time in your server's timezone)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:295
msgid ""
"Contact your hosting provider and ask them to increase the PHP "
"max_execution_time setting"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:302
msgid "Privacy &amp; Data"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:308
msgid "Is any of my site data sent to external servers?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:313
msgid ""
"File contents, passwords, user data and scan results are not sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:320
msgid "Where are scan results stored?"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:324
msgid ""
"Only administrators can open the report (on multisite, only super admins)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/settings.php:330
msgid "ShieldScope has no telemetry and no tracking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:47
msgid "Access Control"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: user name (mirrors the WordPress core login error)
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:119
#, php-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Error:</strong> The password you entered for the username %s is "
"incorrect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:129
msgid "Login error messages may reveal whether a username exists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:130
msgid ""
"After a failed login, WordPress says whether the username exists (\"The "
"password you entered for the username ... is incorrect\"). No login_errors "
"filter active during the scan changes that message, so an attacker may be "
"able to confirm usernames before guessing passwords. Some security plugins "
"change the message only on the login page itself; open wp-login.php, try a "
"wrong password and check what it says. Checked by running the login_errors "
"filter on WordPress's own message; no login was attempted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:131
msgid ""
"Use a security or login-protection plugin that shows one generic message for "
"every failed login, or add a login_errors filter that returns a generic "
"message. Limiting login attempts matters more than hiding usernames."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:173
msgid "(no permission check)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: REST namespace, for example "myplugin/v1"
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:183
#, php-format
msgid "Review: REST routes in %s accept writes without a login"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of routes, 2: list of routes
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:186
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d route(s) accept POST, PUT, PATCH or DELETE requests from anyone: %2$s. "
"This is normal for contact forms or webhooks that check their own input, but "
"a route that changes data without a permission check is a vulnerability. "
"Checked by reading the registered routes; no request was sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:190
msgid ""
"Check what each route does. If it should not be public, ask the plugin "
"developer to add a permission_callback that checks current_user_can(); if it "
"is meant to be public, confirm it validates input and uses a nonce or "
"signature where it can."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:269
msgid "Administrator accounts have Application Passwords configured"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of usernames
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:272
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The following administrator accounts have application passwords: %s. Each "
"app password is an independent credential — if leaked it grants full API "
"access with no 2FA challenge."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:275
msgid ""
"Review and revoke unused application passwords via Users → Profile. Apply "
"the principle of least privilege — avoid granting admin-level app passwords."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:283
msgid "Application Passwords are active on user accounts"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of usernames
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:286
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Users with application passwords configured: %s. Review and revoke any that "
"are unused or unrecognised."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:289
msgid ""
"Audit application passwords in Users → Profile and remove any that are no "
"longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:322
msgid "Username exposed via author archive redirect"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: redirect URL
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:325
#, php-format
msgid ""
"/?author=1 redirects to %s, leaking a username to unauthenticated visitors "
"and aiding brute-force targeting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:328
msgid ""
"The redirect goes to the author's URL slug (user_nicename), which WordPress "
"builds from the login, so changing the display name does not help. Block ?"
"author= requests for logged-out visitors with a security plugin or a web-"
"server rule, or give each account a nicename that differs from its login. "
"Limiting login attempts matters more than hiding usernames."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:385
msgid "Login page is publicly accessible without brute-force protection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:386
msgid ""
"wp-login.php is reachable and no recognised login-protection plugin is "
"active. Bots continuously run credential-stuffing attacks against WordPress "
"login pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:387
msgid ""
"Protect your login page by enabling rate limiting at the webserver or "
"firewall level, or by moving wp-login.php to a custom URL (so bots cannot "
"find the default path). Check your hosting dashboard — many managed hosts "
"include brute-force protection built in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:412
msgid "No two-factor authentication plugin detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:413
msgid ""
"No recognised 2FA plugin is active. Without a second factor, a stolen "
"password is sufficient to compromise any account."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:414
msgid ""
"Enable two-factor authentication for all administrator accounts. With 2FA, a "
"stolen password alone is not enough to access an account. Search for \"two-"
"factor\" on wordpress.org/plugins to find a suitable option, or check "
"whether your hosting provider includes 2FA tools in their dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:462
msgid "Review: public AJAX handler with no nonce check in the same file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:466
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Found %d wp_ajax_nopriv_ hook in a file that contains no nonce check. This "
"is a file-level pattern match: the check may live in another file, and some "
"public handlers do not need one. Review the handler to confirm."
msgid_plural ""
"Found %d wp_ajax_nopriv_ hooks in a file that contains no nonce check. This "
"is a file-level pattern match: the check may live in another file, and some "
"public handlers do not need one. Review the handlers to confirm."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:473
msgid ""
"If the handler changes data, it should call check_ajax_referer() or "
"wp_verify_nonce() to prevent cross-site request forgery."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:489
msgid "Review: AJAX handler with no capability or nonce check in the same file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:493
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Found %d wp_ajax_ hook in a file that contains no current_user_can() or "
"nonce check. This is a file-level pattern match: the checks may live in "
"another file. If they are missing, any logged-in user could trigger the "
"action."
msgid_plural ""
"Found %d wp_ajax_ hooks in a file that contains no current_user_can() or "
"nonce check. This is a file-level pattern match: the checks may live in "
"another file. If they are missing, any logged-in user could trigger the "
"actions."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-access-control.php:500
msgid ""
"Call current_user_can() with the required capability and use "
"check_ajax_referer() or wp_verify_nonce() to prevent CSRF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:154
msgid "plugin and theme code not scanned: Developer review is off in Settings"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: file path
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:427
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:226
#, php-format
msgid "Could not analyse: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:428
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:227
msgid ""
"A pattern check failed on this file (the regular expression engine hit a "
"limit), so the file was not fully checked. Very large or unusual files can "
"cause this, and so can files written to avoid pattern checks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:429
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:228
msgid ""
"Open the file and review it by hand, or compare it with the original plugin "
"or theme source."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of files, 2: number of folders
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:565
#, php-format
msgid "%1$d file(s) and %2$d folder(s) not scanned"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:572
msgid "Some files were not scanned"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of folders, 2: number of symlinked folders, 3: number of files
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-base.php:575
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Folders skipped (vendor, node_modules, .git): %1$d. Symlinked folders not "
"followed: %2$d. Files skipped (too large or unreadable): %3$d."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:68
msgid "Code Pattern Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:210
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:746
msgid "Matches pattern: eval() on encoded data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:211
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:747
msgid ""
"This file applies eval() to the output of a decode or decompress function "
"(base64_decode, gzinflate, str_rot13 or gzuncompress). Malware often uses "
"this shape, but some legitimate libraries and installers do too. This match "
"has not been confirmed as harmful."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:212
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:748
msgid ""
"Compare the file with the original plugin or theme source. If it does not "
"belong there, remove it and check the site for other changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:256
msgid "Matches pattern: shell command function"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:257
msgid ""
"This file calls shell_exec, passthru, proc_open, popen or system. Some "
"plugins use these legitimately, for example backup or image tools. This "
"match has not been confirmed as harmful."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:258
msgid ""
"Check that the plugin needs the call and that no request data reaches the "
"command without escapeshellarg()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:268
msgid "Matches pattern: include/require of request data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:269
msgid ""
"An include or require statement appears to use $_GET, $_POST, $_REQUEST or "
"$_COOKIE directly. If the value is not checked first, this can allow file "
"inclusion. This match has not been confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:270
msgid ""
"Open the file and check that the value is limited to a fixed list of allowed "
"paths before it is included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:300
msgid "Matches pattern: request data in a database query string"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:301
msgid ""
"A $wpdb query string appears to contain $_GET, $_POST, $_REQUEST or $_COOKIE "
"data without $wpdb->prepare(). If the value is not sanitised earlier, this "
"can allow SQL injection. This match has not been confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:303
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Use $wpdb->prepare() with placeholders (%s, %d, %f). Never concatenate user "
"input into SQL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:313
msgid "Matches pattern: echo of request data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:314
msgid ""
"This file appears to echo $_GET, $_POST, $_REQUEST or $_COOKIE data without "
"escaping. If the value reaches the page as-is, this can allow cross-site "
"scripting (XSS). This match has not been confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:315
msgid ""
"Wrap the value in esc_html(), esc_attr() or wp_kses() depending on the "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:325
msgid "Matches pattern: file_put_contents() with request data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:326
msgid ""
"A file_put_contents() call appears to receive $_GET, $_POST, $_REQUEST or "
"$_FILES data. If the path or content is not checked, this can allow "
"arbitrary file writes. This match has not been confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:327
msgid ""
"Use wp_handle_upload() and validate destination paths with realpath against "
"an allowed base."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:338
msgid "Matches pattern: long encoded string"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:339
msgid ""
"The file contains a base64-shaped string of 400 or more characters. Such "
"strings are often legitimate (images, fonts, SVG), but can also hide a "
"payload. This match has not been confirmed as harmful."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-code-patterns.php:340
msgid "Open the file and inspect the string context."
msgstr ""

