#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:256
msgid "HTTP requests are not redirected to HTTPS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:257
msgid ""
"The site uses HTTPS but plain HTTP requests are not automatically "
"redirected. Visitors who type the address without \"https://\" will have an "
"unencrypted connection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:258
msgid ""
"Add a permanent HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect in your webserver config (.htaccess "
"RewriteRule for Apache, return 301 for Nginx). This is separate from "
"FORCE_SSL_ADMIN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:264
msgid "HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect uses a non-permanent status code"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: HTTP status code
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:267
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The HTTP-to-HTTPS redirect uses a %d (temporary) status code instead of 301. "
"Browsers will not cache it and search engines will not pass full link equity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-components.php:270
msgid "Change the redirect to a 301 Permanent in your webserver configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:30
msgid "HTTP Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:103
msgid "X-Frame-Options header not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:104
msgid ""
"Without this header the site can be iframed by third parties — clickjacking "
"risk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:105
msgid ""
"Send 'X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN' or set a Content-Security-Policy frame-"
"ancestors directive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:109
msgid "X-Content-Type-Options header not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:110
msgid "Browsers may MIME-sniff responses, which enables certain XSS vectors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:111
msgid "Send 'X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff'."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:115
msgid "Referrer-Policy header not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:116
msgid "Full URLs may leak in the Referer header to third-party sites."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:117
msgid "Send 'Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin'."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:121
msgid "HSTS (Strict-Transport-Security) not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:122
msgid ""
"Without HSTS, a browser that follows an http:// link to this site can be "
"downgraded to plain HTTP by a network attacker before the redirect to HTTPS. "
"Once a browser has received the header over HTTPS, it uses HTTPS for this "
"site until max-age expires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:123
msgid ""
"Send 'Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000' over HTTPS. Add "
"includeSubDomains only after confirming every subdomain serves HTTPS, "
"because browsers will refuse plain HTTP on all of them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:127
msgid "Content-Security-Policy (CSP) header not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:128
msgid ""
"Without a CSP, browsers will execute any inline script or load resources "
"from any origin. A missing CSP significantly increases the impact of XSS "
"vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:129
msgid ""
"Define a Content-Security-Policy header in your webserver config or via a "
"plugin. Start with a report-only policy to avoid breaking the site: 'Content-"
"Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src \\'self\\''."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:133
msgid "Permissions-Policy header not set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:134
msgid ""
"Without this header, third-party scripts embedded in the page can request "
"access to browser features such as the camera, microphone, and geolocation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:135
msgid ""
"Send 'Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()' to "
"disable unused browser features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:156
msgid "X-XSS-Protection header enables the legacy XSS filter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:157
msgid ""
"Browsers have removed or deprecated this filter, and where it still runs it "
"can introduce cross-site scripting into otherwise safe pages. Content-"
"Security-Policy is the replacement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:158
msgid ""
"Send 'X-XSS-Protection: 0' or omit the header, and use a Content-Security-"
"Policy instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:185
msgid "WordPress version disclosed in HTML meta"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:186
msgid ""
"The generator meta tag reveals the exact WP version to visitors and "
"automated vulnerability scanners."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:187
msgid ""
"Add to functions.php or an mu-plugin: remove_action('wp_head', "
"'wp_generator');"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:229
msgid "WordPress version exposed via REST API root endpoint"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: WordPress version
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:232
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The /wp-json response body contains the WordPress version string (%s). "
"Automated vulnerability scanners query this endpoint to fingerprint the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:235
msgid ""
"Remove the version from the REST API response by filtering the rest_index "
"data, or remove the generator link from wp_head to reduce fingerprinting "
"surface."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:270
msgid "WordPress version exposed in RSS feed generator tag"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:271
msgid ""
"The RSS feed includes a <generator> tag with the exact WordPress version. "
"Any visitor or bot can read this without authentication."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:272
msgid ""
"Remove the generator tag with: add_filter('the_generator', "
"'__return_empty_string');"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:312
msgid "Plugin/theme version numbers exposed in asset URLs"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of assets with version query strings
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:315
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%d enqueued scripts/styles include ?ver= query parameters pointing to wp-"
"content assets. These expose exact plugin and theme version numbers, helping "
"attackers match installed software against known CVEs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-config.php:318
msgid ""
"Remove version strings from asset URLs with this code in an mu-plugin or "
"your theme's functions.php: function myprefix_remove_asset_ver( $src ) "
"{ return remove_query_arg( 'ver', $src ); } add_filter( 'style_loader_src', "
"'myprefix_remove_asset_ver', 9999 ); add_filter( 'script_loader_src', "
"'myprefix_remove_asset_ver', 9999 ); Note: this also removes cache-busting, "
"so visitors may see old files after an update."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:80
msgid "WordPress Core Integrity"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:148
msgid "Core integrity check skipped — non-standard WordPress build"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: detected environment reason
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:151
#, php-format
msgid ""
"This site appears to be running a modified WordPress distribution (%s). Its "
"core files intentionally differ from the official WordPress.org release, so "
"checksum verification would report false positives and has been skipped. Run "
"this check on your production hosting environment instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:164
msgid "Core version not detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:165
msgid "Could not read $wp_version — skipping core integrity verification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:192
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:210
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:226
msgid "Core integrity check skipped"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: error message
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:195
#, php-format
msgid "Could not reach the WordPress.org checksums API: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:198
msgid ""
"Ensure outbound HTTPS to api.wordpress.org is allowed, then re-run the scan."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: HTTP status
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:213
#, php-format
msgid ""
"WordPress.org returned HTTP %d with no usable checksum data. This usually "
"means the exact WP version / locale combination is not indexed (e.g. nightly "
"builds)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:227
msgid "The WordPress.org checksums response was malformed or empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:261
msgid "core files not verified: WordPress.org checksums unavailable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:378
msgid "Core files differ from the official WordPress build en masse"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: differing count, 2: total count
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:381
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d of %2$d core files do not match the official WordPress.org checksums. "
"Differences at this scale almost always mean the installation is a modified "
"distribution (WordPress Playground, a hosting-customised build) or a version/"
"locale mismatch — not individual file tampering. Individual per-file "
"findings have been suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:385
msgid ""
"If this is a local, staging, or Playground environment, this is expected — "
"re-run the scan on production. On a production site, verify your exact "
"WordPress version and locale, then go to Dashboard → Updates and click \"Re-"
"install now\" to restore official core files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:399
msgid "Missing WordPress core file"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: relative path
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:402
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The core file %s is listed in the WordPress.org checksums but is not present "
"on disk. It may have been deleted or the installation is incomplete."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:405
msgid ""
"Go to Dashboard → Updates and click \"Re-install now\" — this re-downloads "
"all core files without touching your content, plugins, or wp-config.php. "
"Alternatively, download the matching WordPress version from wordpress.org/"
"download/releases and upload just the missing file via FTP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:414
msgid "Modified WordPress core file"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: path, 2: expected hash, 3: actual hash
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:417
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The core file %1$s does not match the hash published on WordPress.org. "
"Expected %2$s, got %3$s. This is almost always a sign of either a manual "
"edit (don't do that) or a compromise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:422
msgid ""
"Download a clean copy of the same WordPress version from wordpress.org/"
"download/releases and compare the file. If you see injected or obfuscated "
"code, your site is compromised — change all passwords, regenerate auth "
"salts, and go to Dashboard → Updates to click \"Re-install now\" to restore "
"all core files safely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:436
msgid "Additional core file differences (summarised)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: count
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:439
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%d further core files differ from the official checksums but were not "
"individually listed to keep the report readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:442
msgid ""
"Go to Dashboard → Updates and click \"Re-install now\" to restore all "
"official core files, then re-run the scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:462
msgid "WordPress Playground / WebAssembly runtime detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:471
msgid "SQLite database integration detected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:481
msgid "skipped via shieldscope_skip_core_integrity filter"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:516
msgid ""
"core folders not checked for unknown files: WordPress.org checksums "
"unavailable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:554
msgid "Unknown file inside WordPress core directory"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: relative path
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:557
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The file %s is inside a core WordPress directory but is not part of the "
"official WordPress.org checksums for this version. This is frequently how "
"backdoors hide."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:560
msgid ""
"Open the file in a text editor (read-only) and look for eval(), "
"base64_decode() or obfuscated code, which are common in injected code. If "
"you did not put it there, delete it immediately via FTP or File Manager, "
"then go to Dashboard → Updates and click \"Re-install now\" to verify all "
"core files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:627
msgid ""
"WordPress root not checked for unknown PHP files: core checksums unavailable"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: file name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:638
#, php-format
msgid "Review: unknown PHP file in the WordPress root: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:639
msgid ""
"This PHP file sits next to wp-config.php but is not part of WordPress. Some "
"are legitimate (for example wordfence-waf.php from Wordfence, or a host's "
"health-check file); a file nobody recognises is a common sign of a "
"compromise, because it can be requested directly from the web."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:640
msgid ""
"Find out what added the file. If nobody recognises it, take a backup, remove "
"it, and check the site for other changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:661
msgid "Drop-in in use"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:662
msgid ""
"Drop-ins are files in wp-content that replace parts of WordPress (caching, "
"database, maintenance and error pages). They are usually added by a caching "
"or hosting plugin and do not appear in the Plugins screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:663
msgid ""
"Confirm each drop-in belongs to a plugin or host you use. Remove drop-ins "
"left behind by plugins you deleted."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: file name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:671
#, php-format
msgid "Review: unknown PHP file in wp-content: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:672
msgid ""
"WordPress only expects index.php and known drop-ins directly inside wp-"
"content. Other PHP files there are sometimes left by plugins, and sometimes "
"planted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:673
msgid "Find out what added the file and remove it if it is not needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:686
msgid "Must-use plugin present"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:687
msgid ""
"Must-use plugins load on every request and cannot be turned off from the "
"Plugins screen. Hosts and some plugins add them legitimately; attackers use "
"them because they are easy to miss."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:688
msgid "Confirm each must-use plugin comes from your host or a plugin you use."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of files, 2: folder
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core-integrity.php:716
#, php-format
msgid "only the first %1$d PHP files in %2$s were checked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:30
msgid "WordPress Core"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:102
msgid "WordPress core is out of date"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: current version, 2: new version
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:105
#, php-format
msgid "You are running WordPress %1$s; version %2$s is available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:109
msgid ""
"Back up your site first (use your host's backup tool or export a database "
"dump), then go to Dashboard → Updates and click \"Update Now\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:119
msgid "WordPress core is up to date"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: version string
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:122
#, php-format
msgid "Running WordPress %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:137
msgid "Theme/plugin file editor is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:138
msgid ""
"The built-in editor lets administrators run arbitrary PHP from the "
"dashboard. If an admin account is compromised, the entire site can be "
"backdoored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:139
msgid "Add to wp-config.php: define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:147
msgid "File modifications from the dashboard are allowed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:148
msgid ""
"DISALLOW_FILE_MODS is not set. Consider disabling plugin/theme installation "
"and updates via the dashboard in strict environments."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:149
msgid ""
"Add to wp-config.php: define('DISALLOW_FILE_MODS', true); — note this also "
"blocks automatic updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:158
msgid "FORCE_SSL_ADMIN is not enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:159
msgid ""
"The site uses HTTPS, but WordPress does not force logins and the admin area "
"onto it. With FORCE_SSL_ADMIN set, WordPress redirects any plain-HTTP login "
"or wp-admin request to HTTPS, so passwords and admin cookies are never sent "
"in the clear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:160
msgid "Add to wp-config.php: define( 'FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true );"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:168
msgid "Automatic updates are fully disabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:169
msgid ""
"Automatic minor/security updates are disabled. Unpatched vulnerabilities "
"will stay unpatched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:170
msgid ""
"In wp-config.php, remove the line or change it to: "
"define('AUTOMATIC_UPDATER_DISABLED', false); This re-enables automatic "
"security patch updates for minor releases. If intentionally disabled, commit "
"to a regular manual update schedule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:210
msgid "Short authentication keys or salts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:211
msgid ""
"One or more AUTH/NONCE keys or salts in wp-config.php are shorter than 40 "
"characters. WordPress uses these values as they are to sign login cookies "
"and nonces, so short values are easier to guess."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:212
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:223
msgid ""
"Visit https://api.wordpress.org/secret-key/1.1/salt/ to generate 8 fresh "
"random keys, then replace all AUTH_KEY / SALT lines in wp-config.php with "
"the generated block. All active sessions will be logged out — this is "
"expected and safe."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:221
msgid "Authentication keys or salts not set in wp-config.php"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:222
msgid ""
"One or more AUTH/NONCE keys or salts are missing or still the placeholder. "
"WordPress then generates random values and stores them in the database, so "
"login cookies stay protected, but anyone who can read the database (for "
"example from a leaked backup) also gets these values."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:241
msgid "WP_DEBUG is enabled and errors are displayed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:242
msgid ""
"Error messages leak path and software version information to visitors and "
"attackers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:243
msgid ""
"In production, set WP_DEBUG to false, or at minimum set WP_DEBUG_DISPLAY to "
"false and log to a file with WP_DEBUG_LOG."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:249
msgid "WP_DEBUG is enabled (errors hidden)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:250
msgid ""
"Debug logging is on. If debug.log is inside wp-content and not blocked by "
"the webserver, it may be publicly readable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:251
msgid ""
"Disable WP_DEBUG in production and make sure debug.log is not accessible via "
"HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:267
msgid "Default database prefix 'wp_' in use"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:268
msgid ""
"The default prefix is not a vulnerability, and changing it gives little "
"protection against SQL injection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:269
msgid ""
"No action needed. Renaming the tables of an existing site is risky; if you "
"do it, take a full database backup first and update $table_prefix in wp-"
"config.php to match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:285
msgid "Site URL is not HTTPS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:286
msgid ""
"The home or site URL is configured over HTTP. Traffic, including login "
"credentials, can be intercepted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:287
msgid ""
"Get a free SSL certificate via your hosting panel (cPanel, Plesk, or "
"similar) using Let's Encrypt. Once installed, update both WordPress Address "
"and Site Address in Settings → General to https://, and add "
"define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true); to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:301
msgid "XML-RPC is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:302
msgid ""
"XML-RPC is commonly abused for password brute-force (system.multicall) and "
"pingback-based DDoS. If you do not use Jetpack, the mobile app, or XML-RPC-"
"based clients, disable it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:303
msgid ""
"Add to your theme's functions.php or a must-use plugin: "
"add_filter('xmlrpc_enabled', '__return_false'); Or block it at the webserver "
"level: Apache 2.4 .htaccess — <Files xmlrpc.php> Require all denied </"
"Files>. Skip this if you use Jetpack or the WordPress mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:336
msgid "REST API exposes user list to unauthenticated requests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:337
msgid ""
"GET /wp/v2/users returns usernames without authentication, aiding targeted "
"brute-force attempts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-core.php:338
msgid ""
"Block the endpoint in functions.php or a must-use plugin: "
"add_filter('rest_endpoints', function($e){ if(!is_user_logged_in())"
"{ unset($e['/wp/v2/users']); unset($e['/wp/v2/users/(?P<id>[\\d]+)']); } "
"return $e; });"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:30
msgid "Database"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:85
msgid "Administrator created in the last 7 days"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: login, 2: date
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:88
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Administrator '%1$s' was created on %2$s. If you did not create this "
"account, your site may be compromised."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:92
msgid ""
"If you did not create this account, treat it as a compromise. Delete it via "
"Users → All Users, change all admin passwords, and regenerate your auth "
"salts in wp-config.php (get fresh keys at https://api.wordpress.org/secret-"
"key/1.1/salt/). Contact your host if you cannot determine how the account "
"was created."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:108
msgid "Open registration with administrator default role"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:109
msgid ""
"Anyone can register and is automatically granted administrator. WordPress "
"does not ship with this setting, so it is a common sign of compromise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:110
msgid ""
"Go to Settings → General and either disable \"Anyone can register\" or "
"change the default role from Administrator to Subscriber. Then go to Users → "
"All Users, filter by Administrator, and delete any accounts you do not "
"recognise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:123
msgid "siteurl and home point to different domains"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: siteurl, 2: home
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:126
#, php-format
msgid ""
"siteurl (%1$s) and home (%2$s) resolve to different hosts. Some sites are "
"set up this way on purpose, but a changed value can also be a sign of "
"compromise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:130
msgid ""
"Go to Settings → General and verify both WordPress Address and Site Address "
"point to your own domain. If either was changed to an unknown domain, revert "
"it and change all admin passwords immediately. Also check wp-config.php for "
"WP_HOME or WP_SITEURL constants that may be overriding the values."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:152
msgid "Review: obfuscated JavaScript in stored content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:157
msgid "Review: hidden iframe in stored content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:162
msgid "Review: script tag in stored content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:189
msgid "This option"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: post type, 2: post ID
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:203
#, php-format
msgid "This %1$s (ID %2$d)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:235
msgid ""
"contains a <script> tag. Page builders, analytics and embeds add scripts "
"legitimately; injected spam and redirect code also hides here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:236
msgid ""
"contains code that is typical of injected spam or redirects. Legitimate "
"content rarely needs it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:237
msgid "This is a pattern match, not a confirmed infection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-database.php:238
msgid ""
"Open the item in the editor (or the options table) and check the code. If "
"nobody added it, remove it and change administrator passwords."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:35
msgid "Filesystem & Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:113
msgid "wp-config.php is world-readable"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: octal permissions
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:116
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Permissions on wp-config.php are %s, so every account on the server can read "
"the database credentials. This matters on shared servers; some hosts need "
"this setting for PHP to read the file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:119
msgid ""
"If PHP runs as the file owner, change permissions to 0640 or 0600 (chmod 640 "
"wp-config.php). Check with your host first and load the site after the "
"change."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: label
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:154
#, php-format
msgid "%s directory is world-writable"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: path, 2: octal
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:157
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Directory %1$s has permissions %2$s. Any user on the server can write to it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:161
msgid ""
"Change permissions to 0755 (directories) / 0644 (files) or stricter, owned "
"by the web user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:180
msgid "readme.html is publicly accessible"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:181
msgid ""
"The file discloses the WordPress version, helping attackers match known CVEs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:182
msgid ""
"Delete readme.html from your WordPress root via FTP or your hosting File "
"Manager. Since it is recreated on each core update, also block it "
"permanently in Apache .htaccess: <Files readme.html> deny from all </Files>. "
"For Nginx: location = /readme.html { deny all; }"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:211
msgid "Review: PHP file inside uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:212
msgid ""
"The uploads folder should only hold media and documents. A PHP file there "
"can be run by anyone who requests it, which is a common way to keep access "
"to a hacked site. Some plugins store PHP files in uploads for their own use, "
"so check what this file is before acting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:213
msgid ""
"Do not open the file in a browser. Find out which plugin created it; if none "
"did, take a backup, delete it, change all administrator passwords and check "
"the site for other changes. To stop PHP from running in uploads: on Apache "
"2.4 put \"Require all denied\" inside a <FilesMatch \"\\.ph(p[0-9]?|tml|ar)$"
"\"> block in wp-content/uploads/.htaccess; on Nginx add a location rule that "
"denies \\.php requests under /wp-content/uploads/ (ask your host)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:283
msgid "Backup file can be downloaded from the web"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:284
msgid "Backup file in the web root"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: filename
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:288
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%s is in the site root and the web server sends its contents to anyone who "
"requests it. It is likely to contain database credentials or a full copy of "
"the site data."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: filename
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:293
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%s is in the site root. The web server did not serve it when checked, but a "
"server or plugin change could expose it; files like this often contain "
"database credentials or site data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:297
msgid ""
"Delete the file or move it outside the web root now, then change the "
"database password (in wp-config.php and in your hosting panel) and any keys "
"it contained."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:298
msgid "Move the file outside the web root or delete it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:322
msgid "wp-config.php is publicly readable and contains credentials"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:323
msgid ""
"A request to /wp-config.php returned HTTP 200 and the response body contains "
"database constants (DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD). Your database "
"credentials are exposed to anyone on the internet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:324
msgid ""
"Block access to wp-config.php at the webserver level immediately. Apache: "
"add a <Files wp-config.php> deny from all </Files> block. Nginx: add "
"\"location ~* wp-config\\.php { deny all; }\". Also rotate your database "
"password immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:351
msgid "license.txt is publicly accessible"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:352
msgid ""
"The WordPress license file is accessible and discloses the WordPress version "
"in its copyright year/version line."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:353
msgid ""
"Delete license.txt from the webroot, or block it at the webserver level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:358
msgid "wp-activate.php is publicly accessible"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:359
msgid ""
"The wp-activate.php file is reachable from the internet. On single-site "
"WordPress it serves no purpose and its content includes the WordPress "
"version in the page title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:360
msgid ""
"Block access to wp-activate.php at the webserver level unless you are "
"running WordPress Multisite with email-based user activation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:365
msgid ".htaccess file is publicly accessible"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:366
msgid ""
"The .htaccess file returned HTTP 200. It may contain rewrite rules, "
"directory configurations, or access controls that expose your site structure "
"and configuration to attackers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:367
msgid ""
"Ensure your webserver is configured to block direct access to dotfiles. For "
"Apache, add: <FilesMatch '^\\.'> deny from all </FilesMatch>"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:403
msgid "Directory listing enabled on uploads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:404
msgid "Visitors can enumerate every file under wp-content/uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:405
msgid ""
"Add \"Options -Indexes\" to your root .htaccess file to disable directory "
"listings site-wide. For Nginx, add \"autoindex off;\" inside your server "
"block. You can also place an empty index.php file in the uploads directory "
"as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: directory label e.g. "wp-content/plugins"
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:434
#, php-format
msgid "Directory listing enabled on %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: directory label
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:439
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The %s directory returns a browsable file listing. Attackers can enumerate "
"all installed plugins and themes, then match them to known CVEs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-filesystem.php:442
msgid ""
"Add 'Options -Indexes' to the root .htaccess file (Apache) or 'autoindex "
"off;' in the Nginx server block. Placing an empty index.php in each "
"directory also suppresses listing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:60
msgid "Injection Vulnerabilities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:153
msgid ""
"This is a pattern match, not a confirmed vulnerability: read the code to "
"confirm whether request data really reaches this call."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:173
msgid "PHP Object Injection: deserialization of direct user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:174
msgid ""
"unserialize() or maybe_unserialize() appears to be called directly on "
"request data. A crafted serialized payload can instantiate objects and, with "
"a suitable gadget chain, lead to code execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:175
msgid ""
"Do not deserialize request data. Use json_decode() for data interchange. If "
"deserialization is unavoidable, pass allowed_classes => false."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:179
msgid "Variable variable injection from user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:180
msgid ""
"Using $$_GET or $$_POST creates variable names from request data, which lets "
"a visitor overwrite variables in scope."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:181
msgid ""
"Remove variable variables on request data. Read keys explicitly against an "
"allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:185
msgid "Mass variable extraction from user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:186
msgid ""
"extract() on request data injects visitor-chosen keys into the current "
"variable scope."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:187
msgid ""
"Remove extract() on request data. Read keys explicitly: $foo = "
"sanitize_text_field( wp_unslash( $_POST['foo'] ?? '' ) );"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:191
msgid "call_user_func() with user-controlled callable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:192
msgid ""
"Request data appears in a call_user_func() call. If it selects the function "
"name, a visitor can call any PHP function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:193
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:310
msgid "Check the callable against a strict allowlist before calling it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:197
msgid "SQL injection: sprintf() building $wpdb query with user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:198
msgid ""
"sprintf() with request data inside a $wpdb query does not escape SQL values."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:200
#, php-format
msgid "Use $wpdb->prepare() with %s / %d / %f placeholders."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:204
msgid "SQL injection: superglobal interpolated in $wpdb query string"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:205
msgid ""
"A superglobal appears to be interpolated directly into a $wpdb query string."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:206
msgid "Use $wpdb->prepare(); never interpolate request data into SQL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:210
msgid "XSS: printf() echoing unescaped user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:211
msgid ""
"printf() or vprintf() appears to output request data without an escaping "
"function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:212
msgid ""
"Escape with esc_html(), esc_attr() or esc_url() before passing values to "
"printf()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:216
msgid "XSS: superglobal interpolated inside echoed string"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:217
msgid ""
"A superglobal appears to be interpolated inside an echoed double-quoted "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:218
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:309
msgid ""
"Escape with esc_html(), esc_attr() or esc_url(), depending on the output "
"context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:222
msgid "LDAP injection: LDAP query function called with user input"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:223
msgid ""
"Request data appears in an LDAP query call, which allows the query to be "
"changed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:224
msgid "Escape with ldap_escape() (LDAP_ESCAPE_FILTER or LDAP_ESCAPE_DN)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:228
msgid "XXE risk: SimpleXML parsing user-supplied XML"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:229
msgid ""
"Request data appears to be parsed as XML. If entity substitution is enabled, "
"a crafted document can read local files or make the server send requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:230
msgid ""
"Do not pass LIBXML_NOENT or LIBXML_DTDLOAD when parsing untrusted XML "
"(libxml 2.9 and later do not load external entities by default). Reject "
"documents that contain a DOCTYPE."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:253
msgid "Deprecated create_function() — potential code injection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:254
msgid ""
"create_function() works like eval() and was removed in PHP 8. If request "
"data reaches its arguments it allows code execution; on PHP 8 the call is a "
"fatal error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:255
msgid "Replace it with an anonymous function (closure)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:265
msgid "preg_replace() /e modifier — code injection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:266
msgid ""
"The /e modifier runs the replacement as PHP code. It was removed in PHP 7.0, "
"so on current PHP the call fails; on old PHP it is a code-execution risk."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:267
msgid "Replace with preg_replace_callback()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:304
msgid ""
"Deserializing request data can instantiate objects (PHP object injection)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:304
msgid "Use json_decode() instead, or pass allowed_classes => false."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:304
msgid "unserialize()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:305
msgid ""
"Pass the value as a $wpdb->prepare() argument with a typed placeholder, or "
"cast it with absint() first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:305
msgid ""
"The variable appears in the SQL text of a $wpdb query rather than as a $wpdb-"
">prepare() argument."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:305
msgid "a $wpdb query"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:306
msgid "Remove eval(); plugin code almost never needs it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:306
msgid "Request data reaching eval() would be code execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:306
msgid "eval()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:307
msgid ""
"Do not pass request data to shell functions. If unavoidable, use "
"escapeshellarg() and a strict allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:307
msgid ""
"Request data reaching a shell function would allow OS command execution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:307
msgid "a shell function"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:308
msgid "A file path chosen by request data allows local file inclusion."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:308
msgid ""
"Map request values to a fixed list of files; never build an include path "
"from request data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:308
msgid "include/require"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:309
msgid "Echoing request data without escaping is cross-site scripting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:309
msgid "echo"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:310
msgid "A callable chosen by request data can call any PHP function."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:310
msgid "call_user_func()"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: dangerous call, for example "eval()"; 2: PHP variable name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:324
#, php-format
msgid "Review: user input near %1$s (%2$s)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: PHP variable name, 2: dangerous call, 3: why it matters, 4: review note
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:327
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$s is assigned from request data and later appears in %2$s in the same "
"file. %3$s %4$s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:440
msgid ""
"Trace each maybe_unserialize() call in this file. Confirm its argument comes "
"from stored data (database, options, meta) and never from request data, and "
"that AJAX handlers check a nonce and a capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:445
msgid ""
"Review: user input near maybe_unserialize() in a file with an "
"unauthenticated AJAX action"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:446
msgid ""
"This file registers a wp_ajax_nopriv_ action (reachable by logged-out "
"visitors) and also deserializes data. If request data reaches the "
"deserialization call, that would be PHP object injection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:454
msgid "Review: user input near maybe_unserialize()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:455
msgid ""
"This file reads request data and also calls maybe_unserialize() on a value "
"that is not obviously stored data. If request data reaches that call, it "
"would be PHP object injection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:463
msgid ""
"Review: user input near maybe_unserialize() in a file with an AJAX action"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:464
msgid ""
"This file registers an AJAX action and calls maybe_unserialize(). If a "
"logged-in user with few permissions can send data that reaches the call, it "
"would be PHP object injection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:475
msgid "Review: user input near wp_parse_str()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:476
msgid ""
"wp_parse_str() turns a query string into an array of visitor-chosen keys. "
"Code that uses those keys without checking them can be steered by the "
"request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:477
msgid ""
"Read only the keys you expect from the resulting array and sanitise each one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:498
msgid "PHP register_globals is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:499
msgid ""
"register_globals automatically injects GET/POST/COOKIE values as global "
"variables, enabling variable injection across the entire codebase."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:500
msgid ""
"Disable register_globals in php.ini immediately. It was removed from PHP 5.4."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:509
msgid "PHP allow_url_include is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:510
msgid ""
"allow_url_include lets include/require load code from remote URLs, so a file-"
"inclusion bug in any plugin becomes remote code execution. On its own it is "
"not an exploit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-injection.php:511
msgid "Set allow_url_include = Off in php.ini."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:30
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:95
msgid "Plugin update available"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: name, 2: current, 3: new
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:98
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Plugin \"%1$s\" is at version %2$s; %3$s is available. Outdated plugins are "
"the single most common WordPress compromise vector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:103
msgid ""
"Go to Dashboard → Updates and update this plugin. Check the changelog for "
"the word \"security\" to understand what's fixed. Outdated plugins are the "
"leading cause of WordPress compromises — do not delay security updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:125
msgid "Inactive plugin present on disk"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:128
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Plugin \"%s\" is installed but not active. Its code is still on disk and "
"could be exploited if it has a vulnerability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:131
msgid ""
"Go to Plugins → Installed Plugins and click Delete — not just Deactivate. "
"Inactive plugins leave code on disk that can still be exploited if they "
"contain vulnerabilities. Only keep plugins you actively use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:154
msgid "Plugin has no update source declared"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:157
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Plugin \"%s\" declares neither a PluginURI nor an UpdateURI. If this is not "
"a custom plugin, verify it came from a trusted source."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:160
msgid ""
"Search wordpress.org/plugins to verify this plugin is legitimate. If it's a "
"custom-built plugin, this warning can be ignored. If it came from a \"free "
"premium plugin\" site, treat it as a possibly nulled (pirated) copy, which "
"often carries injected code, and delete it — replace with the official "
"version from the original developer."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of plugins
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:256
#, php-format
msgid "%d plugin(s) could not be looked up on WordPress.org"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:278
msgid "not given"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:279
msgid "unknown date"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:283
#, php-format
msgid "Plugin closed on WordPress.org: %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: plugin name, 2: date, 3: reason
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:286
#, php-format
msgid ""
"WordPress.org closed \"%1$s\" on %2$s (reason: %3$s). A closed plugin gets "
"no updates, and WordPress still shows it as up to date. A closure for a "
"security issue usually means a known, unfixed vulnerability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:291
msgid ""
"Replace the plugin with a maintained alternative and delete it. If you must "
"keep it for now, check the plugin's page and support forum on WordPress.org "
"for the reason and any fix."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:309
#, php-format
msgid "Plugin not updated on WordPress.org for over 2 years: %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: plugin name, 2: date
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:312
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The last release of \"%1$s\" on WordPress.org was on %2$s. Plugins without "
"updates do not get fixes for newly found vulnerabilities and may break with "
"new WordPress or PHP versions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:316
msgid ""
"Check the plugin's support forum for signs of maintenance and look for a "
"maintained alternative. If you keep it, review it whenever WordPress or PHP "
"is updated."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of plugins
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:466
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%d plugin(s) not verified against WordPress.org checksums (not listed there, "
"or no checksums for the installed version)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:494
#, php-format
msgid "Most files of %s differ from WordPress.org"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of files, 2: plugin version
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:497
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d files differ from the WordPress.org release of version %2$s. The "
"installed copy is probably not the official release (a different build or a "
"modified copy), so individual files were not listed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:501
msgid ""
"Reinstall the plugin from WordPress.org (Plugins → deactivate, delete, "
"reinstall), or confirm where this copy came from."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:513
#, php-format
msgid "Plugin file differs from the WordPress.org release: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:515
msgid ""
"This PHP file is not identical to the same file in the official release of "
"the installed version. Someone changed it after installation: a local edit, "
"or injected code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:516
msgid ""
"This file is not identical to the same file in the official release of the "
"installed version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:517
msgid ""
"Compare the file with the official release. If nobody on your team edited "
"it, reinstall the plugin from WordPress.org and check the site for other "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:537
#, php-format
msgid "Review: many PHP files not in the WordPress.org release: %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of files, 2: plugin version, 3: example paths
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:540
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%1$d PHP files in this plugin folder are not part of the WordPress.org "
"release of version %2$s, for example: %3$s. The installed copy is probably a "
"different build (for example a development or premium version); individual "
"files were not listed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:545
msgid ""
"Confirm where this copy came from, or reinstall the plugin from "
"WordPress.org."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:555
#, php-format
msgid "Review: PHP file not in the WordPress.org release: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-plugins.php:556
msgid ""
"This PHP file is inside the plugin folder but is not part of the official "
"release of the installed version. Some plugins write cache or configuration "
"files; a file nobody recognises can be a planted backdoor."
msgstr ""

