#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:372
msgid ""
"Disable TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1 in your web server configuration. For Apache: "
"SSLProtocol all -SSLv3 -TLSv1 -TLSv1.1. For Nginx: ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 "
"TLSv1.3;"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: TLS version label e.g. "TLS 1.0"
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:392
#, php-format
msgid "%s support could not be determined"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: TLS version label, 2: error message
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:398
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The %1$s test connection failed before the server could accept or refuse it, "
"often because this server's own TLS library no longer offers %1$s. Error: "
"%2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: TLS version label
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:404
#, php-format
msgid ""
"The %s test connection completed, but the negotiated TLS version could not "
"be read back, so the result is not reliable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:407
msgid ""
"Check the enabled TLS versions with an external TLS scanner, or in your web "
"server configuration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:514
msgid "Mixed content detected — HTTP resources loaded on HTTPS page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:518
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Found %d HTTP resource reference on the HTTPS homepage. Browsers block or "
"warn on mixed active content (scripts, stylesheets, iframes), reducing page "
"security to HTTP level."
msgid_plural ""
"Found %d HTTP resource references on the HTTPS homepage. Browsers block or "
"warn on mixed active content (scripts, stylesheets, iframes), reducing page "
"security to HTTP level."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssl.php:525
msgid ""
"Replace all HTTP asset URLs with HTTPS equivalents. Check plugin/theme "
"settings, hardcoded URLs in the database (use Better Search Replace to "
"update), and ensure WordPress Address and Site Address both use https://."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:48
msgid "Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:126
msgid ""
"This is a pattern match, not a confirmed vulnerability: read the code to "
"confirm whether request data really chooses the destination."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:131
msgid "Review: user input near wp_remote_*() (possible SSRF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:132
msgid ""
"Request data appears in a WordPress HTTP API call. If it sets the URL, a "
"visitor can make the server send requests to internal hosts such as cloud "
"metadata endpoints or localhost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:133
msgid ""
"Use wp_safe_remote_get() and check the host against an allowlist before "
"sending the request."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:137
msgid "Review: user input near wp_safe_remote_*()"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:138
msgid ""
"wp_safe_remote_*() rejects private and loopback addresses, which covers most "
"server-side request forgery. Redirects and DNS changes can still reach "
"unexpected hosts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:139
msgid ""
"If the destination comes from the request, also check the host against an "
"allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:143
msgid ""
"Review: user input near file_get_contents() (possible file read or SSRF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:144
msgid ""
"Request data appears in a file_get_contents() call. If it sets the path, a "
"visitor could read local files, or make the server fetch URLs when "
"allow_url_fopen is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:145
msgid ""
"Map request values to a fixed list of files. For HTTP, use "
"wp_safe_remote_get() with a host allowlist."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:149
msgid "Review: user input near cURL CURLOPT_URL (possible SSRF)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:150
msgid ""
"Request data appears where a cURL URL is set. If it sets the URL, a visitor "
"can make the server send requests to internal hosts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:151
msgid ""
"Check the host against an allowlist and reject private and loopback "
"addresses, or use wp_safe_remote_get()."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:155
msgid "Review: user input near a socket connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:156
msgid ""
"Request data appears in fsockopen() or stream_socket_client(). If it sets "
"the host, a visitor can make the server open connections to any host."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:157
msgid ""
"Check the host against an allowlist and reject private, loopback and link-"
"local addresses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:161
msgid "Review: user input near wp_redirect() (possible open redirect)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:162
msgid ""
"Request data appears in wp_redirect(). If it sets the destination, the site "
"can be used to send visitors to any site (phishing)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:163
msgid "Use wp_safe_redirect(), or wp_validate_redirect() with a fallback URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:167
msgid "Review: user input near a Location header (possible open redirect)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:168
msgid ""
"Request data appears in a Location header. If it sets the destination, the "
"site can be used to send visitors to any site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:169
msgid "Use wp_safe_redirect() with a fallback URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:220
msgid "oEmbed proxy answered a logged-out request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:221
msgid ""
"The /wp-json/oembed/1.0/proxy endpoint makes the server fetch a URL and "
"return the result. WordPress core only allows it for users with the "
"edit_posts capability, but it answered a request sent without a login, so a "
"plugin or filter has probably opened it up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:222
msgid ""
"Find the plugin or code that changes the proxy's permission check. If you do "
"not need the oEmbed REST routes, remove them: "
"remove_action( 'rest_api_init', 'wp_oembed_register_route' );"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:231
msgid "Pingbacks are allowed on new posts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:232
msgid ""
"New posts accept pingbacks through XML-RPC. To check a pingback, WordPress "
"fetches the source URL the sender supplies, so anyone can make the server "
"send requests to URLs they choose. Pingbacks have been used for DDoS "
"reflection and to probe internal hosts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:233
msgid ""
"If you do not use pingbacks, go to Settings → Discussion and clear 'Allow "
"link notifications from other blogs (pingbacks and trackbacks) on new "
"posts'. Existing posts keep their own setting. Turning off XML-RPC removes "
"pingbacks completely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:242
msgid "PHP allow_url_fopen is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:243
msgid ""
"allow_url_fopen lets file_get_contents() and similar functions fetch remote "
"URLs. Combined with any path-traversal or injection bug that passes a URL to "
"file_get_contents(), this becomes an SSRF vector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:244
msgid ""
"Set allow_url_fopen = Off in php.ini if your code does not intentionally use "
"file_get_contents() for HTTP requests (use wp_remote_get() instead)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:253
msgid "WooCommerce webhooks may be configured — review webhook URLs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:254
msgid ""
"WooCommerce supports webhooks that cause the server to make outbound HTTP "
"requests. A compromised admin account could add a webhook pointing at an "
"internal service, enabling SSRF."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-ssrf.php:255
msgid ""
"Review active webhooks in WooCommerce → Settings → Advanced → Webhooks. "
"Ensure only trusted external URLs are configured."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:30
msgid "Themes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:78
msgid "Theme update available"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: name, 2: version
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:81
#, php-format
msgid "Theme \"%1$s\" has an update to version %2$s available."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:85
