"child theme first. Child theme customisations are not affected by parent "
"theme updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:110
msgid "Multiple inactive themes installed"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: count
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:113
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%d inactive themes are present. Keep only your active theme, its parent (if "
"any), and one up-to-date default theme as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:116
msgid ""
"Go to Appearance → Themes and delete all themes you are not using — keep "
"only your active theme, its parent (if any), and one default WordPress theme "
"as a fallback. Inactive themes on disk can still be exploited even without "
"being active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:136
msgid "No current default theme installed as fallback"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:137
msgid ""
"If your active theme breaks, WordPress falls back to a default theme. "
"Without one installed, recovery requires FTP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-themes.php:138
msgid ""
"Install one of the current default (Twenty*) themes and keep it updated."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:30
msgid "Users & Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:79
msgid "An administrator named 'admin' exists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:80
msgid "Attackers often try the username 'admin' first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:81
msgid ""
"Go to Users → Add New and create a new Administrator with a unique username. "
"Log in as the new admin, then delete the old \"admin\" account — on the "
"deletion screen choose \"Attribute all content to\" your new account to "
"transfer all posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:104
msgid "Unusually high number of administrators"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: count
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:107
#, php-format
msgid ""
"%d administrator accounts exist. Each is a potential point of compromise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:110
msgid ""
"Go to Users → All Users, filter by Administrator, and review each account. "
"Downgrade accounts that do not need full access — change their role to "
"Editor (content management) or Author (own posts only) via their profile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:147
msgid "Non-standard password hash detected"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: login
#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:150
#, php-format
msgid ""
"User '%s' has a password hash that does not match WordPress' phpass or "
"bcrypt format. This may be a legacy md5/sha1 hash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/checks/class-shieldscope-check-users.php:153
msgid ""
"Force a password reset: go to Users → All Users, edit the user, generate a "
"new password, and save — the hash upgrades to a modern format automatically "
"on next login. If the account is unrecognised, delete it immediately and "
